[data-can-leave] Anything this agent reads ($ROOT/home/Documents/research and whatever your "BRAVE_SEARCH_KEY" unlocks on api.search.brave.com) can be sent to api.search.brave.com (acting as you) and any public hostname. The fetch tool's GET requests are not prompted and can carry data out in the URL.
This agent:
- uses a model you pick at launch.
- can read $ROOT/home/Documents/research (at /workspace/research); can write there with your approval; cannot delete there.
- can reach api.search.brave.com on port 443, any public hostname on port 443 (through the Sallyport proxy only).
- can send up to 1MiB in one request body the proxy reads, for fetch and at hosts with a credential grant (default 8MiB).
- can receive up to 16MiB in one response body the proxy reads, for fetch and at hosts with a credential grant (default 64MiB).
- can hold up to 16 proxy connections open at once (default 32).
- uses your BRAVE_SEARCH_KEY secret only toward api.search.brave.com, sent as the header "X-Subscription-Token" in the form "{value}" (the agent never sees the value).
- cannot run shell commands.
- fetch sends GET and HEAD requests without asking you. A GET can still change things at a host. At a host with a credential grant it carries that credential.
- may call: fs_read, fs_list, fs_write, fetch.
- up to 3 approval requests can wait at once; more are denied (default 5).
- is limited to 2 CPUs, 4GiB memory, 256 processes, and 2h of wall time.
